    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d301">

                <pb facs="0448" n="356" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v01/pg356"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72119/2138</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Russia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Francis</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Archangel</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-10-12T18:00:00+03:31">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 12, 1918, 6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received October 13, 6 a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>471. To President Wilson:</p>
                <p>Sir: We hope you include Russia, while replying to Germany’s request for
                    armistice, among Powers whose territories [are] to be cleared of invaders, since
                    we have repudiated treaty of Brest Litovsk and continued at war with Central
                    Powers. We consider ourselves allies of you and other Allied Powers. Signed,
                    President Government Northern Russia, member Ufa Directory of Five, Nicholas
                    Tchaikowski.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Francis</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
